+// group_pick_scale — the director's group-scoped demand weight (permille): a
+// source terminal that is a member of an ESTATE (cluster size >= min_members)
+// picks at (1000 + (size-1) × member_weight_permille)/1000 of its
+// demand_weight; a sub-min cluster (a singleton/duo — not yet an estate)
+// keeps 1000 (no bonus). Aggregate group demand rises as members join: every
+// member beyond the first adds member_weight_permille to the estate's pick
+// weight. Pure function of catalog data (deterministic; integer, ODN-10).
+group_pick_scale :: proc(cat: ^Catalogs, size: i32) -> i32 {
+	if size < cat.balance.growth_groups.min_members {
+		return 1000
+	}
+	return 1000 + (size - 1) * cat.balance.growth_groups.member_weight_permille
+}
